# The octoflow-gate release (https://github.com/DavidSiegl/octoflow-gate/releases) that judges this repository's
# changes, as ci/fetch-gate.sh reads it: one line, the release's version and the sha256 of its
# octoflow-gate-<version>.tar.gz, as the release's .sha256 asset gives it. A build reads this file from its own tree
# (the Jenkinsfile's Gate stage), and the engine is built with its line as BUILT_IN_PIN (engine/src/local_gate.rs), the
# release that judges a project without a pin of its own. Raise it with `cargo xtask raise-gate-pin`, which checks the
# release and changes what goes with it; lower it the same way to roll back to an earlier one, 0.7.0 or later: the
# Gate stage runs a release's `gate`, which the ones before do not ship, so going below 0.7.0 means reverting the
# commit that raised the pin to it with the Gate stage. The release named here must read this commit's gate.toml,
# which refuses keys it does not know.
